comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T14:58:58.446Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete 2840-item all-status corpus and Bun merge-driver lineage reviewed. pm-vks66s closed with valid Bun 1.4.2 evidence; this is a genuine published 2026.9.29 recurrence under Bun 1.3.5, linked by recurs_from. Reproduced in a disposable npm-installed project with both PM tracker roots isolated: Bun 1.3.5 and pm 2026.9.29, merge install exit 0, strict health exit 1 with five driver drifts. Configured executable was a Bun temporary runtime path; no private project data was used."
  "2026-09-29T14:59:19.958Z","harness:codex","Test-audit contract: a bunx --bun process must persist a durable version-matched Bun executable in Git config. Existing test covers matching PATH and Node; extend it with a matching absolute npm_execpath and only mismatched Bun on PATH, so the old fallback fails before repair. Manual acceptance uses the actual published Bun 1.3.5 binary and a packed pm artifact in a temporary Git project, then a real branch merge. No mock replaces install/audit behavior."
  "2026-09-29T15:00:23.959Z","harness:codex","Red phase: focused worktree-config test exited 1 on the new Bun runner-hint assertion. Four existing tests passed. With PATH containing only a mismatched Bun and a matching absolute npm_execpath, the installer fell back to the Node executable in the simulated test, mirroring the published Bun 1.3.5 transient fallback seen in the disposable consumer."
  "2026-09-29T16:16:31.380Z","harness:codex","Green and acceptance evidence 2026-09-29: linked worktree-config test passed 5/5 (pm test run test-local-mumvnf45-fpgu6j). Canonical full coverage passed 9,433 tests with 2 Windows-only skips, exact 65,983/65,983 statements, 50,533/50,533 branches, 13,644/13,644 functions, and 63,006/63,006 lines. Typecheck, security scan, docs links, generated contracts and public surface, record integrity, graph composition, and bounded mutation admission passed; full static chain awaits final rerun after tracker closure. Final packed tarball SHA-256 f950a566da4691af29c38c065e0d0377ad2623616998acc0f763216daaf8eb7f installed by Bun 1.3.5 in a disposable Git project with isolated PM_PATH/PM_GLOBAL_PATH. Bun/bunx and npx executed version 2026.9.29; init, repeated merge install, and strict health passed with zero findings. A real divergent branch merge used the packed Bun driver, preserved right description and left note, verified three history entries with matching item hash, reconciled, and returned strict health ok. Published 2026.9.29 data also read and verified under the packed build. This is packed-artifact evidence, not proof of a future published release."
  "2026-09-29T16:43:50.804Z","harness:codex","Delivery gate status 2026-09-29: pnpm quality:static has not completed locally because the host-sensitive performance subgate failed on different attempts. SDK merge import measured 247 and 231 ms against 226 ms; unchanged main in an isolated built worktree measured 312 ms against the same ceiling, while the candidate later passed the same direct 10-entrypoint gate. A later static attempt passed import cost but failed CLI transport floors (get 381>362 ms, context 445>433, next 469>440, create 424>398, claim 420>415). No threshold was changed. Hosted exact-head static and performance checks remain required before merge; this note does not claim a full local static pass."
  "2026-09-29T17:26:51.751Z","harness:codex","PR #1353 review correction: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1353#discussion_r4136070608 correctly identified directly invoked stable Bun outside PATH. The extended real-Git test failed with merge_bun_launcher_unavailable before repair (exit 1); after repair all 11 focused SDK tests passed. The executing binary is now a candidate after runner/PATH hints, matched by version, while resolved bun-node-* temporary copies are rejected. Test fixtures cover stale PATH, npm_execpath, direct stable execution, and disposable-copy refusal without replacing install/audit behavior. Filesystem/process failures remain candidate-local; the policy extraction meets unchanged ESLint complexity limits."
  "2026-09-29T18:05:34.126Z","harness:codex","Packed review-fix acceptance passed (exit 0, 111344 ms) against @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.9.29 tarball SHA256 1f1f39adc2281bc7eac5e8b2ad41196792686fa07ced48d038872fc736378dd1. npm install/npx --no-install and Bun 1.3.5 add/x --bun --no-install all executed that artifact/version under isolated PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH with telemetry opted out. Direct absolute Bun outside PATH without npm_execpath installed durable drivers; real divergent Git merge retained the left note/right description and three-event strictly verified history; reconcile and strict health passed. A real bun-node disposable binary was refused with merge_bun_launcher_unavailable (exit 5) before Git config/fence writes, then stable direct Bun recovered successfully. Published 2026.9.28 data/history remained readable. This is packed-artifact acceptance, not published-release verification."
  "2026-09-29T18:19:48.840Z","harness:codex","Release-policy reconciliation: current npm and GitHub release are 2026.9.29. Same-day auto-release replay run 36546064282 succeeded after detecting the immutable target and skipped analyzer/build/dependency preparation; only one 2026.9.29 tag/release exists. Hosted concurrency remains cancel-in-progress=false in its shared auto-release group. This patch has not been merged or published; no extra release or manual dispatch was used. Final typecheck, context evaluation, version policy, compatibility, package artifact, 89-command package-first dogfood, packed npx smoke, defect evidence, and bounded two-module mutation admission all exit 0. Linked merge tests pass. The complete coverage rerun is still required."
  "2026-09-29T18:57:02.867Z","harness:codex","Final packed consumer acceptance exits 0 (30720 ms), tarball SHA256 e164bf16c0574db13a3cb75df3c45ff0bae093789d054b7b24daf3a0cfd80112. npm/npx and Bun/bunx executed 2026.9.29; their local bin links resolve to the installed tarball entry, and npx/bunx independently proved the changed full Task-parent behavior, rather than relying on version text alone. Bun 1.3.5 real driver merge, strict history/health, disposable refusal before writes, stable recovery, and published 2026.9.28 data compatibility all pass. Typed temporary authoring consumes sdk/authoring and sdk/testing public exports: typecheck and 2 tests pass; archive install, contracts, dispatch and strict health pass. Local directory source scanning correctly refused its 10000-entry bound and its advertised npm pack archive recovery succeeded. Doctor activation/load/blocking failures are zero; its strict exit 1 accurately reports partial remote-update coverage for this local archive. That warning is not misreported as full update verification."
  "2026-09-29T19:18:54.455Z","harness:codex","Current full validation is not yet green: Node 24.12.0 two-worker run passed previous timeout cases but failed two unchanged output contracts because of experimental SQLite warnings. A Node 26.9.0 two-worker full run now preserves all assertions, deadlines, inventory and exact coverage requirements. Focused, actual packed consumer, previous-data, public authoring, security and bounded mutation evidence remains valid; no current full-suite or merged/published claim is made."
  "2026-09-29T19:37:43.849Z","harness:codex",External delivery evidence remains pending.
  "2026-09-29T19:49:35.618Z","harness:codex",External delivery evidence remains pending.
  "2026-09-29T19:51:19.452Z","harness:codex","Final canonical validation on Node 26.9.0/Vitest 4.1.11: node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage -- --maxWorkers 2 exits 0 after 1229.00 seconds with 9434 passes and two Windows-only skips. All 758 maintained authoring sources are included. Exact coverage is statements 65988/65988, branches 50538/50538, functions 13645/13645, lines 63011/63011, with zero uncovered counts. Complete pnpm quality:static exits 0, including unchanged documentation/export, ESLint, duplication, generated contracts, SDK/public-surface, performance, graph, record integrity and bounded mutation gates. Actual packed npm/npx/Bun/bunx and typed public authoring acceptance passes. Await current-head review; these are implementation and test results, not merge or publication evidence."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-29T18:22:44.986Z","harness:codex","Runtime identity is a valid launcher candidate when a stable Bun binary is invoked directly outside PATH. Version-match and realpath candidates, reject known disposable bunx copies, and prove both pre-write refusal and actual configured Git-driver execution with the historical runtime and packed artifact."
